"Then, in a browser, open http://localhost:8080.\n"
"You should get something like:"
msgstr ""

msgid "As you can see, the endpoint runs on a virtual thread."
msgstr ""

msgid "It's essential to understand what happened behind the scene:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus creates the virtual thread to invoke your endpoint (because of the "
"`@RunOnVirtualThread` annotation)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the code invokes the rest client, the virtual thread is blocked, BUT "
"the carrier thread is not blocked (that's the virtual thread _magic touch_)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Once the first invocation of the rest client completes, the virtual thread "
"is rescheduled and continues its execution."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The second rest client invocation happens, and the virtual thread is blocked "
"again (but not the carrier thread)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Finally, when the second invocation of the rest client completes, the "
"virtual thread is rescheduled and continues its execution."
msgstr ""

msgid "The method returns the result. The virtual thread terminates."
msgstr ""

msgid "The result is captured by Quarkus and written in the HTTP response"
msgstr ""

msgid "Verify pinning using tests"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the `pom.xml,` we added an `argLine` argument to the surefire and "
"failsafe plugins:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `-Djdk.tracePinnedThreads` dumps the stack trace if a virtual thread "
"cannot be _unmounted_ smoothly (meaning that it blocks the carrier thread).\n"
"That's what we call _pinning_ (more info in xref:./virtual-threads."
"adoc#pinning[the virtual thread reference guide])."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend enabling pinning detection in tests.\n"
"Thus, you can check that your application behaves correctly when using "
"virtual threads.\n"
"Just check your log after having run the test.\n"
"If you see a stack trace (on Java 21-23) or pinning events (using the junit-"
"virtual-threads extension), better check what's wrong.\n"
"If your code (or one of your dependencies) pins, it might be better to use "
"regular worker threads instead."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create the `src/test/java/org/acme/TheBestPlaceToBeResourceTest.java` class "
"with the following content:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is a straightforward test, but at least it will detect if our application "
"is pinning.\n"
"Run the test with either:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`r` in dev mode (using continuous testing)"
msgstr ""

msgid "`./mvnw test`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As you will see, it does not pin - no stack trace.\n"
"It is because the REST client is implemented in a virtual-thread-friendly "
"way."
msgstr ""

msgid "The same approach can be used with integration tests."
msgstr ""

